<If you've been letting your pet get ahead of you, it takes a *lot* of
<patience to clean out a shop, because you probably have no treats to
<train it with.

I usually step into shops and search them before I let the pet in. 
A bit dangerous with mimics, but they are slow and generally can be
outrun. 

Any shop that has food will be searched for tripe for treats.

Even without it you can manage with a few simple tricks:

1) Pile everything of no interest in the far corner of the shop.
2) put a cursed item on the top of the pile. The pet won't go
near it.
3) Put the items of interest (expensive spellbooks, IDed gems,
high price potions/wands/scrolls, and cash of course). The pet
will eventually pick them up and bring them out of the shop.
4) Never pay the shopkeep cash. Always drop the cash and pay with
credit.
5) Talk to your pet and never let it get hungry. If necessary
walk the pet around and let it eat.

Again it takes some time to do, but the results are well worth it.

